    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n111290" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῐλομάθ-εια</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[μᾰ]</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>love of
			learning</i> or <i>knowledge, curiosity,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				499e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ti.</u>
				90b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1117b29
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλομαθείας χάριν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					14.1.16
				</span></i>
			: in codd. of <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
			</span></i> l.c. and later writers (as <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Mort.</u>
				33
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Asp.
				<u>in EN</u>
				88.9
			</span></i>) freq. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-μᾰθία. -έω,</span></b> 
			<i>to be fond of learning, eager after knowledge,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				810a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				1.13.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Mort.</u>
				38
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Corn.
				<u>ND</u>
				14
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. περί τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					3.59.4
				</span></i>
			.</div>
